# Routing control-plane graph

Companion to [CONTRACT-TO-RUNTIME-TRACEABILITY.md](CONTRACT-TO-RUNTIME-TRACEABILITY.md).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  TASK[Issue / task declaration] --> CONTRACT[issue-dispatch/v1]
  CONTRACT --> ADMIT[QUE admission]
  TIERS[queue.dispatch-tiers/v2] --> ADMIT
  ADMIT --> EXEC[Swarm dispatch workflow]
  CATALOG[desk-feed/v1.3 provider catalog] --> POOL[DoE-governed pool]
  POOL --> SCOUT[Scout task-fit selection]
  SCOUT --> EXEC
  EXEC --> STAMP[Canonical routed-dispatch stamp]
  STAMP --> FAN[stamp_fanout.py]
  FAN --> DOE[3L0 / DoE / MVT / ATES]
  FAN --> MONEY[MoneyBall]
  FAN --> TRAVERSAL[Desk traversal evidence]
  MODEL[model_router.py / provider-invoke / llm_api_hub] -. receipt enforcement unresolved .-> EXEC
  QUE[QUE collector / governor] --> QFEED[QUE feeds]
  WATCH[Dispatch watchdog] --> WFEED[dispatch-state-feed/v1]
  DESK[Tribute Desk read-only projection] --> QFEED
  DESK --> WFEED
  DESK --> TRAVERSAL
```

## Edge semantics

- `declares`: issue metadata describes task intent and constraints.
- `admits`: QUE evaluates eligibility, tier and dependency rules.
- `assigns`: DoE determines allocation, rotation, treatment and endpoint-level evidence gates.
- `selects`: Scout chooses a task-fit endpoint from the assigned eligible pool and emits the selection receipt.
- `dispatches`: Swarm sends work to the selected execution surface.
- `stamps` / `fans out`: evidence is recorded once and distributed to evaluation planes.
- `projects`: the Desk renders independently generated feeds without executing work.
- `receipt-handoff-unresolved`: the receipt schema is defined, but runtime enforcement from Scout through provider invocation is not yet implemented.
